    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for the info. i'm looking at the bags now and seeing different mixes. if i go with something high in nitrogen to get the color back, am i gonna mess up the root health or cause more of that purplish stuff? also, how often should i be applying it? i don't want to overdo it and burn the grass.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Applying too much high-nitrogen fertilizer too quickly can definitely scorch the grass and potentially exacerbate stunted growth by leading to excessive top growth without healthy roots. To avoid issues, it's best to apply fertilizer in multiple, lighter doses throughout the growing season rather than one heavy application. Monitor your lawn closely after each application, as consistent feeding is key to ensuring steady, balanced nutrient uptake without causing burn.",
      "source": "target",
